# Build and tool output. These are ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose: a bare
# `images` pattern matches at every depth, and it silently swallowed src/scenes/images/
# and src/content/images/ — the whole images course — out of the first commit. The local
# build was fine because the files were on disk; CI caught it on a fresh clone.
/node_modules
/dist
/dist-snapshot
/out
/.tmp
/segments
/images
/frames

*.local
.claude
.DS_Store
